{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This type is used to register a route tree with a router instance. Doing so unlocks the full type safety of TanStack Router, including top-level exports from the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/react-router"},{"type":"text","value":" package."}]},{"type":"code","value":"export type Register = {\n  // router: [Your router type here]\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To register a route tree with a router instance, use declaration merging to add the type of your router instance to the Register interface under the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"router"},{"type":"text","value":" property:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const router = createRouter({\n  // ...\n})\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/react-router' {\n  interface Register {\n    router: typeof router\n  }\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThis type is used to register a route tree with a router instance. Doing so unlocks the full type safety of TanStack Router, including top-level exports from the `@tanstack/react-router` package.\n\n```tsx\nexport type Register = {\n  // router: [Your router type here]\n}\n```\n\nTo register a route tree with a router instance, use declaration merging to add the type of your router instance to the Register interface under the `router` property:\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nconst router = createRouter({\n  // ...\n})\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/react-router' {\n  interface Register {\n    router: typeof router\n  }\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: RegisterType\ntitle: Register type\n---\n\nThis type is used to register a route tree with a router instance. Doing so unlocks the full type safety of TanStack Router, including top-level exports from the `@tanstack/react-router` package.\n\n```tsx\nexport type Register = {\n  // router: [Your router type here]\n}\n```\n\nTo register a route tree with a router instance, use declaration merging to add the type of your router instance to the Register interface under the `router` property:\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nconst router = createRouter({\n  // ...\n})\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/react-router' {\n  interface Register {\n    router: typeof router\n  }\n}\n```\n"}
